1
00:00:07,424 --> 00:00:10,635
I did nothing in the end.

2
00:00:11,428 --> 00:00:13,680
Will I be scolded?

3
00:00:23,648 --> 00:00:28,445
You worked too hard compared to me.

4
00:00:30,697 --> 00:00:32,032
Oh, man.

5
00:00:37,954 --> 00:00:39,706
So pitiful.

6
00:00:46,254 --> 00:00:48,923
Shall I let you rest easy now?

7
00:00:51,384 --> 00:00:52,635
Good job.

8
00:00:54,012 --> 00:00:56,306
You're just a human. Don't act recklessly.

9
00:00:56,931 --> 00:00:57,891
I'll kill you.

10
00:00:57,974 --> 00:01:01,394
You're so annoying.
I just want to help him.

11
00:01:01,478 --> 00:01:03,897
Curses can't understand my kindness?

12
00:01:12,030 --> 00:01:13,782
So where are the goods?

13
00:01:15,116 --> 00:01:16,701
I got them.

14
00:01:18,745 --> 00:01:21,539
Special Grade Cursed Relic, Ryomen Sukuna.

15
00:01:22,248 --> 00:01:24,125
Jujutsu High School has six fingers.

16
00:01:25,168 --> 00:01:28,588
Another Special Grade Cursed Relic,
Cursed Womb, Death Paintings.

17
00:01:29,297 --> 00:01:31,257
Number one to three.

18
00:01:32,926 --> 00:01:35,178
Most of the shrines in Jujutsu High School

19
00:01:35,261 --> 00:01:37,388
are just disguises.

20
00:01:37,472 --> 00:01:41,601
The setting changes every day
according to Tengen's barrier techniques.

21
00:01:43,478 --> 00:01:44,979
Among thousands of doors,

22
00:01:45,063 --> 00:01:46,606
only one leads to the vault

23
00:01:46,689 --> 00:01:51,861
where highly dangerous cursed objects
like Sukuna's fingers are kept.

24
00:01:57,992 --> 00:02:02,539
Only Tengen knows which door
leads to the vault on that day.

25
00:02:02,622 --> 00:02:04,415
No one should hinder you.

26
00:02:04,499 --> 00:02:06,376
Who is Tengen?

27
00:02:06,459 --> 00:02:09,170
A Jujutsu Sorcerer with immortality
as his cursed technique.

28
00:02:09,254 --> 00:02:10,213
Immortality?

29
00:02:10,296 --> 00:02:12,549
Compared to Satoru Gojo, who is stronger?

30
00:02:12,632 --> 00:02:14,926
He has eternal life,
but he will continue to age.

31
00:02:15,510 --> 00:02:17,929
Just treat him like a tree.

32
00:02:18,721 --> 00:02:20,807
Besides opening the barrier,

33
00:02:20,890 --> 00:02:22,851
he hardly interferes with the world.

34
00:02:22,934 --> 00:02:24,644
You don't have to bother about him.

35
00:02:26,020 --> 00:02:28,940
When we let Jujutsu High School
collect the finger back then,

36
00:02:29,732 --> 00:02:34,195
I placed a talisman created by
Mahito's cursed energy on it first.

37
00:02:34,696 --> 00:02:36,614
I placed it
on the first layer of the seal.

38
00:02:36,698 --> 00:02:38,449
It won't peel off.

39
00:02:39,033 --> 00:02:41,077
You can find it easily.

40
00:02:41,161 --> 00:02:42,787
Are there any guards?

41
00:02:42,871 --> 00:02:46,541
From the entrance to the vault,
there are two followers of Tengen.

42
00:02:46,624 --> 00:02:47,792
They are small fries.

43
00:02:48,418 --> 00:02:49,419
Forget them.

44
00:02:49,502 --> 00:02:51,379
Before the Veil is lifted,

45
00:02:51,462 --> 00:02:55,884
I hope you can eliminate Jujutsu Sorcerers
who are on standby as quietly as possible.

46
00:02:55,967 --> 00:02:57,552
I want to ease Hanami's burden.

47
00:02:57,635 --> 00:02:58,553
Sure.

48
00:02:59,053 --> 00:03:02,974
Why don't we seal Satoru Gojo
inside the Veil?

49
00:03:03,892 --> 00:03:07,979
I don't want him to focus on Mahito,
which is our main goal.

50
00:03:11,566 --> 00:03:16,112
Besides, I can't test the Veil
if he doesn't use his full strength.

51
00:03:16,195 --> 00:03:18,656
Trapping the students is the easiest way.

52
00:03:18,740 --> 00:03:22,118
Everyone except Sukuna's vessel
can be killed?

53
00:03:22,201 --> 00:03:24,495
Yes, but I don't recommend it.

54
00:03:24,579 --> 00:03:25,747
What?

55
00:03:27,582 --> 00:03:32,253
Sukuna's behavior is quite different
from what I imagined.

56
00:03:32,962 --> 00:03:35,465
This is just my guess,

57
00:03:36,716 --> 00:03:41,512
but I'm afraid some students there
might be landmines for Sukuna.

58
00:03:43,264 --> 00:03:44,641
If we step on the landmines,

59
00:03:44,724 --> 00:03:48,394
the worst-case scenario is that
this mission will be in vain.

60
00:03:48,478 --> 00:03:51,689
Can't we just kidnap Itadori first?

61
00:03:51,773 --> 00:03:53,399
He's quite useful anyway.

62
00:03:53,483 --> 00:03:55,276
No way. Itadori…

63
00:03:55,360 --> 00:03:57,654
Sukuna himself is a time-bomb,

64
00:03:57,737 --> 00:04:00,740
for us and Jujutsu High School.

65
00:04:05,036 --> 00:04:10,041
I want to wait until the chaos
worsens to provoke him.

66
00:04:12,001 --> 00:04:15,588
October 31st, Shibuya.

67
00:04:16,506 --> 00:04:18,883
In order to seal Satoru Gojo,

68
00:04:18,967 --> 00:04:21,803
we must keep the things
that are useful first.

69
00:04:25,765 --> 00:04:29,435
A few Curse Users will tag along.

70
00:04:29,519 --> 00:04:32,480
You can abandon Juzo Kumiya.

71
00:04:32,563 --> 00:04:35,608
He's not the kind
who will follow through with the plan.

72
00:04:35,692 --> 00:04:37,402
He'll hinder us in the future.

73
00:04:38,111 --> 00:04:42,573
Someone else will observe
the test results of the Veil.

74
00:04:42,657 --> 00:04:44,200
Get along well with them.

75
00:04:44,284 --> 00:04:47,912
He asked us to get along well, Jogo.

76
00:04:47,996 --> 00:04:49,831
I won't be going anyway.

77
00:04:54,252 --> 00:04:56,087
Come on. Wake up, Hanami.

78
00:04:56,587 --> 00:04:57,714
Let's go back.

79
00:04:58,464 --> 00:05:00,133
-Mahito.
-What?

80
00:05:02,093 --> 00:05:05,888
It's stressful for curses
to quell their killing intent.

81
00:05:10,518 --> 00:05:13,062
You're sounding more like a Cursed Spirit.

82
00:06:43,986 --> 00:06:45,154
KYOTO JUJUTSU HIGH SCHOOL

83
00:06:45,238 --> 00:06:46,948
Next up will be casualties.

84
00:06:47,990 --> 00:06:51,744
Three Grade 2 Jujutsu Sorcerers,
one Semi-Grade 1 Jujutsu Sorcerer,

85
00:06:51,828 --> 00:06:53,371
five supervisors,

86
00:06:53,454 --> 00:06:55,081
and two treasury guards.

87
00:06:55,164 --> 00:06:57,083
They are the Jujutsu Sorcerers on standby

88
00:06:57,166 --> 00:07:01,170
working separately
under Mr. Gojo and Principal Yaga.

89
00:07:01,254 --> 00:07:03,923
Although we're still waiting
for Ms. Ieiri's report,

90
00:07:04,006 --> 00:07:05,758
we're positive that it's done by

91
00:07:05,842 --> 00:07:08,594
the Cursed Spirit that
Mr. Nanami encountered previously.

92
00:07:08,678 --> 00:07:09,679
Damn it.

93
00:07:09,762 --> 00:07:14,809
Should we let the students and other
Jujutsu Sorcerers know about this?

94
00:07:15,935 --> 00:07:17,103
No.

95
00:07:17,186 --> 00:07:19,647
Limit this news among the superiors.

96
00:07:19,730 --> 00:07:21,065
I don't want the Curse Users

97
00:07:21,149 --> 00:07:24,318
to know about the missing
Special Grade Cursed Relics.

98
00:07:24,402 --> 00:07:26,571
Did the Curse User say anything?

99
00:07:26,654 --> 00:07:27,864
Well…

100
00:07:27,947 --> 00:07:30,241
Although he can't keep a secret,

101
00:07:30,324 --> 00:07:34,078
he didn't provide any useful information.

102
00:07:34,579 --> 00:07:37,498
Regarding this attack,

103
00:07:37,582 --> 00:07:42,211
he said he was just following his orders.

104
00:07:43,212 --> 00:07:46,007
I just wanted to make a clothing rack.

105
00:07:46,507 --> 00:07:50,261
I don't know the monk's name.

106
00:07:50,344 --> 00:07:52,472
I don't even know its gender.

107
00:07:52,555 --> 00:07:54,932
It's a kid with a bob cut and white hair.

108
00:07:56,309 --> 00:07:59,937
A monk child with an unknown gender
and a bob cut?

109
00:08:00,605 --> 00:08:02,023
Any clues?

110
00:08:02,106 --> 00:08:03,357
No.

111
00:08:03,441 --> 00:08:05,109
I guess he made it up.

112
00:08:05,193 --> 00:08:07,487
Do we have anyone
skilled at making people confess?

113
00:08:07,570 --> 00:08:12,658
Why were curses and outsiders able to
sneak past Master Tengen's barrier?

114
00:08:12,742 --> 00:08:15,244
I believe it's due
to that Special Grade Cursed Spirit

115
00:08:15,328 --> 00:08:17,121
who fought with the students.

116
00:08:17,830 --> 00:08:19,665
That Cursed Spirit has a special aura.

117
00:08:20,541 --> 00:08:24,128
It's a Cursed Spirit,
but close to a spirit.

118
00:08:24,212 --> 00:08:27,840
According to Aoi, that guy seems
to be able to submerge into plants.

119
00:08:28,841 --> 00:08:32,512
Master Tengen's barrier
is ineffective against plants, right?

120
00:08:33,095 --> 00:08:37,433
His barrier was designed
to hide rather than protect.

121
00:08:37,517 --> 00:08:40,269
It will be weak once infiltrated.

122
00:08:43,981 --> 00:08:48,694
Are they afraid that Sukuna's finger
will strengthen Yuji's potential?

123
00:08:48,778 --> 00:08:51,822
Or did they do that
to strengthen themselves?

124
00:08:52,865 --> 00:08:55,409
It doesn't make any sense.

125
00:08:55,952 --> 00:08:59,497
Anyway, let's be glad
that the students are safe.

126
00:09:01,457 --> 00:09:04,961
But the Sister-School
Goodwill Event must be canceled.

127
00:09:05,044 --> 00:09:08,506
Wait a minute. It's not for us to decide.

128
00:09:08,589 --> 00:09:09,715
-What?
-What?

129
00:09:11,592 --> 00:09:15,221
When did you become
good friends with that gorilla?

130
00:09:15,304 --> 00:09:18,766
No, we're not really good friends, but…

131
00:09:18,849 --> 00:09:24,188
Although I do have some memories of it,
it felt like I wasn't exactly myself.

132
00:09:24,272 --> 00:09:26,399
What are you talking about?
Were you drunk?

133
00:09:26,482 --> 00:09:30,528
Do you think I can drink
in that situation?

134
00:09:30,611 --> 00:09:31,988
That's shocking.

135
00:09:32,488 --> 00:09:37,034
Fortunately, Fushiguro's injuries
were not serious.

136
00:09:37,118 --> 00:09:38,828
He can even eat pizza.

137
00:09:41,122 --> 00:09:43,958
No, please bring food
that are easy to digest.

138
00:09:45,543 --> 00:09:46,919
Don't complain.

139
00:09:47,753 --> 00:09:51,799
At that time, it seemed better that
my cursed energy was almost used up.

140
00:09:52,300 --> 00:09:55,928
After the roots were removed,
Ms. Ieiri was able to treat my wounds.

141
00:09:56,012 --> 00:09:57,013
Is that so?

142
00:09:57,096 --> 00:09:58,514
So things like that can happen.

143
00:09:58,598 --> 00:10:00,891
Didn't you fight with that Cursed Spirit?

144
00:10:01,767 --> 00:10:02,935
Itadori.

145
00:10:03,019 --> 00:10:04,270
What?

146
00:10:04,353 --> 00:10:06,897
You've gotten stronger.

147
00:10:07,898 --> 00:10:09,400
Back then…

148
00:10:10,568 --> 00:10:15,114
We talked about our own truths.

149
00:10:16,991 --> 00:10:19,243
We both might have been right.

150
00:10:19,327 --> 00:10:23,164
But on the other hand, we're both wrong.

151
00:10:23,247 --> 00:10:24,332
What?

152
00:10:24,415 --> 00:10:26,584
Some questions have no answers, right?

153
00:10:26,667 --> 00:10:28,002
Don't think too much.

154
00:10:28,085 --> 00:10:29,170
You'll get bald.

155
00:10:29,253 --> 00:10:31,547
That's right. There's no answer at all.

156
00:10:31,631 --> 00:10:34,425
Now it all depends on
whether or not we can accept it.

157
00:10:35,384 --> 00:10:38,220
You can't accept it
when you have no sense of self.

158
00:10:38,304 --> 00:10:40,681
A weak Jujutsu Sorcerer
has no sense of self.

159
00:10:43,100 --> 00:10:44,518
I'll get stronger too.

160
00:10:45,770 --> 00:10:47,480
I will surpass you soon.

161
00:10:50,524 --> 00:10:52,443
You are still the same.

162
00:10:52,526 --> 00:10:55,196
Don't talk among yourselves.

163
00:10:55,279 --> 00:10:58,157
This is what I expect
from my brother's friends.

164
00:11:01,619 --> 00:11:04,413
Where are you going, brother?

165
00:11:04,497 --> 00:11:06,082
I'm very grateful to you,

166
00:11:06,165 --> 00:11:07,667
but please let me go!

167
00:11:07,750 --> 00:11:10,252
I was feeling abnormal at that time!

168
00:11:10,336 --> 00:11:12,046
What are you talking about?

169
00:11:12,129 --> 00:11:14,965
You were like that since middle school!

170
00:11:15,049 --> 00:11:18,803
We're not from the same middle school!

171
00:11:21,472 --> 00:11:22,640
CURSE

172
00:11:22,723 --> 00:11:25,142
Hello, I'm the useless Miwa.

173
00:11:25,643 --> 00:11:27,895
I said I'm useless,

174
00:11:27,978 --> 00:11:31,899
but I don't think I'm that useless.

175
00:11:33,651 --> 00:11:35,945
But when a Special Grade
Cursed Spirit attacked us

176
00:11:36,028 --> 00:11:38,614
and everyone was fighting hard,

177
00:11:39,824 --> 00:11:41,951
I was sound asleep.

178
00:11:42,034 --> 00:11:43,744
So I can't say anything.

179
00:11:45,621 --> 00:11:46,747
Also…

180
00:11:46,831 --> 00:11:49,166
Who broke my katana?

181
00:11:49,667 --> 00:11:51,085
Mai's sister?

182
00:11:51,627 --> 00:11:55,131
Many things have happened, and I thought
the Goodwill Event would be canceled.

183
00:11:55,631 --> 00:11:57,883
However, after a day off,

184
00:11:59,427 --> 00:12:00,886
we're now…

185
00:12:01,512 --> 00:12:03,013
The game starts now!

186
00:12:03,097 --> 00:12:04,765
…playing baseball!

187
00:12:16,689 --> 00:12:18,149
ONE DAY AGO

188
00:12:18,232 --> 00:12:19,150
So…

189
00:12:19,233 --> 00:12:22,278
Many things happened,
and some people died.

190
00:12:22,361 --> 00:12:25,156
What do you want to do?
Continue the Goodwill Event?

191
00:12:26,365 --> 00:12:29,160
When you put it like that…

192
00:12:29,243 --> 00:12:30,161
Of course…

193
00:12:30,786 --> 00:12:33,164
We should continue.

194
00:12:34,498 --> 00:12:36,459
Todo…

195
00:12:37,042 --> 00:12:38,461
Why?

196
00:12:38,544 --> 00:12:43,674
First, mourning is only for those
close to the people who have passed away.

197
00:12:43,757 --> 00:12:46,093
That's not our concern.

198
00:12:46,177 --> 00:12:48,888
Second, since people have died,

199
00:12:48,971 --> 00:12:52,641
all the more reason
we should get stronger.

200
00:12:52,725 --> 00:12:55,978
Strength is built based on
the accumulation of results.

201
00:12:56,061 --> 00:12:58,481
Either suffer the defeat
or taste the victory.

202
00:12:58,564 --> 00:13:00,733
That is how we grow.

203
00:13:00,816 --> 00:13:04,737
Results are important
since they are physical proof!

204
00:13:04,820 --> 00:13:08,574
I didn't expect Senior Todo
to be so serious.

205
00:13:08,657 --> 00:13:10,618
He's seriously crazy.

206
00:13:10,701 --> 00:13:14,205
Third, the feeling of
not finishing up things in school

207
00:13:14,288 --> 00:13:16,290
will make you regret it for a lifetime.

208
00:13:16,373 --> 00:13:18,125
How old are you?

209
00:13:18,209 --> 00:13:19,960
I don't really mind.

210
00:13:20,044 --> 00:13:21,378
We will win anyway.

211
00:13:21,462 --> 00:13:23,380
It's ridiculous, but it makes sense.

212
00:13:23,464 --> 00:13:25,007
You should just rest, Kamo.

213
00:13:25,090 --> 00:13:26,383
I have no objection.

214
00:13:26,467 --> 00:13:27,468
Salmon.

215
00:13:27,551 --> 00:13:29,887
Do we decide the individual battles
by drawing lots?

216
00:13:29,970 --> 00:13:31,180
What?

217
00:13:31,263 --> 00:13:33,265
There are no individual battles this year.

218
00:13:35,100 --> 00:13:38,562
The principals of both schools
will propose their own methods of dueling.

219
00:13:38,646 --> 00:13:41,815
Each method takes one day,
so that's two days in total.

220
00:13:41,899 --> 00:13:43,901
And that's the official consensus.

221
00:13:43,984 --> 00:13:47,446
We have group battles on the first day,
and individual battles on the second.

222
00:13:47,530 --> 00:13:48,781
It's always been like this.

223
00:13:48,864 --> 00:13:49,907
Salmon.

224
00:13:52,618 --> 00:13:56,038
I hate to follow a fixed routine.

225
00:13:56,121 --> 00:13:59,792
Every year, the team events
are put in a box and opened on the day.

226
00:14:04,380 --> 00:14:07,591
When Principal Gakuganji held the meeting,

227
00:14:07,675 --> 00:14:10,594
he only confirmed
what was needed for the day.

228
00:14:11,387 --> 00:14:12,304
BASEBALL

229
00:14:12,888 --> 00:14:14,557
What?

230
00:14:14,640 --> 00:14:16,141
-What?
-Oh, my!

231
00:14:16,225 --> 00:14:18,060
-Baseball?
-You're here too?

232
00:14:18,143 --> 00:14:20,354
What's this, Yaga?

233
00:14:20,437 --> 00:14:23,315
No, I'm sure that
I wrote "individual battles."

234
00:14:23,816 --> 00:14:26,068
Wait a minute, Satoru!

235
00:14:28,153 --> 00:14:29,363
CURSE

236
00:14:29,446 --> 00:14:31,574
KASUMI MIWA, SECOND BASEMAN

237
00:14:35,953 --> 00:14:37,329
It's a pop fly!

238
00:14:37,413 --> 00:14:40,708
Nishimiya, don't run first!

239
00:14:42,001 --> 00:14:43,544
Out.

240
00:14:43,627 --> 00:14:44,837
Why?

241
00:14:44,920 --> 00:14:47,214
Just say it if you don't know the rules!

242
00:14:47,298 --> 00:14:49,842
I know the rules!
I run when I hit the ball, right?

243
00:14:51,176 --> 00:14:53,470
Sacrifice fly? What's that?

244
00:14:53,554 --> 00:14:55,014
A new torture method?

245
00:14:55,097 --> 00:14:56,515
You simpleminded fool!

246
00:14:57,182 --> 00:14:59,602
NORITOSHI KAMO, THIRD BASEMAN

247
00:14:59,685 --> 00:15:01,854
I heard that you repelled
the Special Grade.

248
00:15:01,937 --> 00:15:02,897
What?

249
00:15:02,980 --> 00:15:07,109
No, it's all thanks to Todo and Mr. Gojo.

250
00:15:07,192 --> 00:15:08,611
Are you playing with no helmet?

251
00:15:09,820 --> 00:15:13,616
Itadori, why do you want
to be a Jujutsu Sorcerer?

252
00:15:13,699 --> 00:15:15,951
At first, it just happened.

253
00:15:17,036 --> 00:15:20,581
I'm afraid of loneliness,
and I want to help many people.

254
00:15:20,664 --> 00:15:24,251
When I die, I hope many people
will come and pay their last respects.

255
00:15:26,420 --> 00:15:30,257
If Mother is not here,
I don't want to be a Jujutsu Sorcerer!

256
00:15:32,718 --> 00:15:34,887
You're talented, Noritoshi.

257
00:15:35,387 --> 00:15:37,389
You can help many people.

258
00:15:38,474 --> 00:15:41,810
The more people you help,
the more people will acknowledge you.

259
00:15:42,394 --> 00:15:45,856
This way, all kinds of people
will come to help you.

260
00:15:46,649 --> 00:15:48,567
You won't be alone anymore.

261
00:15:49,485 --> 00:15:51,904
When you become a great Jujutsu Sorcerer,

262
00:15:53,489 --> 00:15:55,407
come and pick me up.

263
00:15:58,953 --> 00:16:00,079
I see.

264
00:16:00,663 --> 00:16:03,248
This is a good reason.

265
00:16:03,332 --> 00:16:06,001
Strike! Batter out, change!

266
00:16:06,085 --> 00:16:08,504
Kamo, the ball is not going to hit itself!

267
00:16:09,046 --> 00:16:11,215
TEAM KYOTO: 0

268
00:16:11,298 --> 00:16:14,718
They call me Tohoku's Maakun!

269
00:16:14,802 --> 00:16:17,054
Tohoku's Maakun
is Masahiro Tanaka himself.

270
00:16:17,137 --> 00:16:19,640
-Maakun is a pitcher!
-Bonito flakes!

271
00:16:22,810 --> 00:16:23,727
What?

272
00:16:25,938 --> 00:16:27,606
MECHAMARU

273
00:16:27,690 --> 00:16:29,191
Wait a minute!

274
00:16:29,274 --> 00:16:31,902
Kugisaki is mad. A fight's breaking out!

275
00:16:32,695 --> 00:16:35,114
That's a pitching machine!

276
00:16:35,197 --> 00:16:36,532
What are you talking about?

277
00:16:36,615 --> 00:16:38,826
That's the spare Mechamaru.

278
00:16:38,909 --> 00:16:41,870
Panda broke him the other day.
Of course, we have to use this.

279
00:16:41,954 --> 00:16:44,623
Pitching machine?

280
00:16:44,707 --> 00:16:48,377
I don't know what that is.
Are you familiar with machines?

281
00:16:48,460 --> 00:16:49,753
Are you a geek?

282
00:16:49,837 --> 00:16:53,632
How dare you keep blabbering…

283
00:16:53,716 --> 00:16:56,385
You're a high school student, right?

284
00:16:57,469 --> 00:17:00,848
Bring it! I'll take you on!

285
00:17:01,390 --> 00:17:02,766
She's on the base.

286
00:17:02,850 --> 00:17:04,268
She's really desperate.

287
00:17:06,311 --> 00:17:08,480
MEGUMI FUSHIGURO, OUTFIELDER

288
00:17:13,318 --> 00:17:14,528
Out.

289
00:17:17,114 --> 00:17:19,533
PANDA, FIRST BASEMAN
HOPES TO BEAT UP ZEBRAS ONE DAY

290
00:17:28,792 --> 00:17:30,961
MAKI ZENIN, PITCHER

291
00:17:31,045 --> 00:17:31,962
Damn it.

292
00:17:39,636 --> 00:17:41,221
MECHAMARU

293
00:17:53,275 --> 00:17:54,526
Gosh!

294
00:17:57,237 --> 00:17:59,615
All right, three points.

295
00:18:06,455 --> 00:18:08,749
-That's cheating!
-Bonito flakes!

296
00:18:08,832 --> 00:18:10,501
Kugisaki, come back.

297
00:18:10,584 --> 00:18:13,003
DUE TO LACK OF PLAYERS,
AN OUTFIELDER MAY USE CURSED TECHNIQUE

298
00:18:13,128 --> 00:18:15,047
KYOTO
TOKYO

299
00:18:16,715 --> 00:18:18,008
Catcher, huh?

300
00:18:18,717 --> 00:18:23,013
You receive, pass, read the game,
do fielding, and many more.

301
00:18:23,639 --> 00:18:26,517
It's the perfect position
for you, brother.

302
00:18:27,101 --> 00:18:31,605
But I hope to go head-to-head
with you as the pitcher.

303
00:18:32,231 --> 00:18:33,524
Todo.

304
00:18:34,233 --> 00:18:35,818
You can just be the pitcher.

305
00:18:35,901 --> 00:18:37,069
No.

306
00:18:37,152 --> 00:18:39,947
Only Mechamaru can be the pitcher now.

307
00:18:41,490 --> 00:18:43,200
Promise me, brother.

308
00:18:43,283 --> 00:18:48,163
If I hit a home run here,
it's your turn next to--

309
00:18:51,041 --> 00:18:53,877
DID IT ON PURPOSE

310
00:18:54,837 --> 00:18:58,006
Todo! Pull yourself together!

311
00:18:58,090 --> 00:18:59,508
Nice pitch.

312
00:18:59,591 --> 00:19:01,009
-Nice pitch.
-Nice pitch.

313
00:19:01,093 --> 00:19:02,761
-Nice pitch.
-Maki, nice pitch.

314
00:19:02,845 --> 00:19:05,681
-Nice pitch.
-Nice pitch.

315
00:19:05,764 --> 00:19:10,561
-Nice pitch.
-Nice pitch.

316
00:19:10,644 --> 00:19:12,187
-Todo.
-Nice pitch.

317
00:19:12,271 --> 00:19:14,648
-Everyone…
-Nice pitch.

318
00:19:14,731 --> 00:19:16,650
-They hate you so much.
-Nice pitch.

319
00:19:16,733 --> 00:19:18,485
-Nice pitch.
-Nice pitch.

320
00:19:20,404 --> 00:19:22,823
Do you still hate Itadori?

321
00:19:22,906 --> 00:19:25,576
It's not about hate or love.

322
00:19:25,659 --> 00:19:30,038
According to sorcery rules,
Itadori's existence is forbidden.

323
00:19:30,122 --> 00:19:33,083
He's still alive
because of Gojo's stubbornness.

324
00:19:33,167 --> 00:19:37,421
You shouldn't distort the rules
because of an individual.

325
00:19:37,504 --> 00:19:43,093
Not to mention that Itadori
being alive may cause more deaths.

326
00:19:43,802 --> 00:19:47,890
But it's also true
that he has saved lives.

327
00:19:47,973 --> 00:19:51,852
This time, he cooperated with Todo
to repel the Special Grade Cursed Spirit.

328
00:19:51,935 --> 00:19:54,938
Although such things
are not limited to students,

329
00:19:55,439 --> 00:19:58,692
Itadori will experience
a lot of regrets in the future.

330
00:20:00,068 --> 00:20:01,820
"I should have done that."

331
00:20:01,904 --> 00:20:03,363
"I wish they had done that."

332
00:20:03,447 --> 00:20:05,240
"I should have said that."

333
00:20:05,324 --> 00:20:07,034
"I wish they had said that."

334
00:20:11,246 --> 00:20:16,293
Honestly, I don't know
if the decision on Itadori was right.

335
00:20:18,212 --> 00:20:22,090
But can't we just watch over him for now?

336
00:20:26,762 --> 00:20:27,596
Hey.

337
00:20:27,679 --> 00:20:28,680
He got on base!

338
00:20:28,764 --> 00:20:31,183
Inumaki is fast.

339
00:20:31,266 --> 00:20:32,684
Salted fish roe.

340
00:20:32,768 --> 00:20:34,436
Mai! Miwa!

341
00:20:34,519 --> 00:20:36,021
Be careful of stolen base!

342
00:20:37,272 --> 00:20:39,441
Let's save our regrets…

343
00:20:40,025 --> 00:20:41,693
for later.

344
00:21:01,088 --> 00:21:02,256
We got in.

345
00:21:06,969 --> 00:21:08,136
All right!

346
00:21:13,809 --> 00:21:16,144
30TH SISTER-SCHOOL GOODWILL EVENT
2ND DAY, BASEBALL

347
00:21:16,228 --> 00:21:17,229
TOKYO SCHOOL WINS, 2-0

348
00:21:18,313 --> 00:21:19,356
What?

349
00:21:21,316 --> 00:21:25,070
Yaga, think of a way
to deal with Gojo first.

350
00:22:56,453 --> 00:22:58,371
-Juju Stroll.
-Salmon.

351
00:22:58,455 --> 00:22:59,998
DO YOU PREFER RICE OR BREAD?

352
00:23:00,582 --> 00:23:05,378
Rice? No, I like bread too.

353
00:23:05,462 --> 00:23:07,964
Wait a minute.
Are the ingredients pollack roe?

354
00:23:08,048 --> 00:23:09,091
Rice.

355
00:23:09,674 --> 00:23:11,051
I think it's rice.

356
00:23:11,134 --> 00:23:13,595
What? I would definitely choose bread.

357
00:23:14,179 --> 00:23:15,430
Salted rice balls.

358
00:23:15,514 --> 00:23:18,725
I'm a panda! Of course, I choose bread!

359
00:23:18,809 --> 00:23:20,811
Do you want to get killed?

360
00:23:21,853 --> 00:23:23,355
Was that…

361
00:23:24,189 --> 00:23:27,234
a little far-fetched?

362
00:23:27,734 --> 00:23:29,528
He ran out of jokes.

363
00:23:29,611 --> 00:23:30,862
Time to go back.
